<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Piedmont</h1><p class="st-meta">1294 CE – 1418 CE · capital Pinerolo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Savoy-Achaea principality in Piedmont, a cadet branch of the house of Savoy that also claimed the Frankish Principality of Achaea in Greece.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1294 Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-v-count-of-savoy">Amadeus V</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-savoy">County of Savoy</a> settled his nephew Philip with the family's lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> as a dependent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a>. In 1301 Philip married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-of-villehardouin">Isabella of Villehardouin</a>, heiress of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea</a>, and his line kept the title princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> even after losing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Philip and his heirs ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pinerolo">Pinerolo</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> and the towns of the upper Po plain, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the counts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-savoy">Savoy</a>. They fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/march-of-montferrat">March of Montferrat</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/marquisate-of-saluzzo">Marquisate of Saluzzo</a> for control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> and held assemblies of nobles and towns. Prince Louis founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-turin">University of Turin</a> in 1404.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Louis died without a legitimate heir in 1418, and his lands returned to his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-viii-duke-of-savoy">Amadeus VIII</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-savoy">Duchy of Savoy</a>, uniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-savoy">Savoy</a>. The heir to the Savoy throne was later styled Prince of Piedmont.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1294 CE – 1418 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.45%;width:2.47%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1294 CE – 1418 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pinerolo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Philip of Savoy-Achaea, James of Savoy-Achaea, Louis of Savoy-Achaea</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Piedmontese, Franco-Provençal, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Savoy-Achaea, Principality of Piedmont</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1356&amp;focus=lordship-of-piedmont" aria-label="Lordship of Piedmont on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4855 592 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Piedmont lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5175 848L5140 827M5175 848L5140 827"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5140 827h0M5140 827h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5175 848h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5175 848h0"/></svg></a><figcaption